@page "/privacy"
@page "/privacy-policy"
@attribute [StreamRendering]

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Revalidate</PageTitle>

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<div class="legal-document">
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated: 3 January 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
        Revalidate ("the Service," "we," "us," or "our") is a unified solution to validate Trackmania replays and ghosts remotely that provides replay validation, verification, and analysis services.
    </p>
    <p>
        The Service is part of the gbx.tools ecosystem and relies on <a href="https://identity.gbx.tools">identity.gbx.tools</a> for user authentication and identity management. We do not operate our own account system and do not store credentials.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Authentication and Data Access</h2>
    <p>
        When you sign in on revalidate.gbx.tools, we use a secure, shared authentication cookie issued by identity.gbx.tools to verify your identity. This cookie is essential and we may use it to request additional data from the identity manager as needed to provide functionality.
    </p>
    <p>
        All identity-related data processing, including OAuth provider data, cookies, and account management, is governed by the <a href="https://identity.gbx.tools/privacy">identity.gbx.tools Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Data We Store</h2>
    
    <h3>3.1 User Data</h3>
    <p>
        We can store limited data received from identity.gbx.tools:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>User ID</li>
        <li>Trackmania (2020) and ManiaPlanet player login and nickname</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>3.2 Validation Data</h3>
    <p>
        When you upload replays, ghosts, or maps for validation, we store:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Replay, ghost, and map (.Gbx) files and basic metadata</li>
        <li>Validation results, timing data, checksums, and logs</li>
        <li>Ghost inputs, checkpoint data, and system information available in replay/ghost files</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <p>
        We use collected data to:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Validate replays and ghosts using dedicated server containers</li>
        <li>Generate validation reports</li>
        <li>Improve service accuracy, performance, and security</li>
        <li>Produce anonymous usage statistics</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>
        Validation results and uploaded files are public by default.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>
        Uploaded files, validation results, and related technical data are stored indefinitely to preserve validation integrity.
    </p>
    <p>
        Deleting your account via identity.gbx.tools does not automatically delete historical validation data.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
        We implement appropriate security measures:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Regular security updates and monitoring</li>
        <li>Isolated, containerized validation environments</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
        Your data protection rights, including GDPR rights where applicable, are described in the <a href="https://identity.gbx.tools/privacy">identity.gbx.tools Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        Additionally, you can:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Request deletion of specific validation requests and associated data (with authentication)</li>
        <li>Contact us for data deletion or export requests</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Updates to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our services or legal requirements. Continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or data deletion requests, please contact us through the <a href="https://discord.gbx.tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gbx.tools Discord server</a> or via GitHub issues on the <a href="https://github.com/BigBang1112/revalidate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Revalidate repository</a>.
    </p>
</div>